# Agent harness

This is a single-repo **agent harness**. This git tree holds
orchestration rules, living plans, domain memory, measurement loops,
and product code.

This is a shareable template. Do not record harness-internal planning
in `_plans/` or `_plans/DECISIONS.md`. Standing harness rules live in
`CLAUDE.md`, skills, and `.claude/prompt-snippets/`.

Do not add a `repos/` clone manager. Put product code in this tree,
or copy these harness files into an existing app repo.

## Skills

Workspace skills live in `.claude/skills/` and are mirrored under
`.cursor/skills/`. Keep the two trees identical.

Harness skills:

- `/create-plan` / `/implement-plan` — spec-first execution
- `/eval-loop` — one observe → hypothesize → test → keep/kill cycle
- `/mount-production-db` — production dump → throwaway sidecar Postgres
- `/commit` — stage and commit this repo. Never push.
- `/update-all-md-docs` — refresh markdown so links stay accurate

## Git

- Never `git push`. Never open SSH. The user pushes.
- A project hook blocks `git push`, `ssh`, and `git commit --no-verify`.
- Isolated worktrees: `scripts/worktree_agent.sh <branch>`. Clean with
  `--clean <branch>`. Do not pass a `repos/` name.
- Git ignores `_local/eval.env` (sidecar secrets). See `README.md`.
- Ignore Postgres MCP connection failures unless the user asked for
  `/eval-loop`, `/mount-production-db`, or sidecar SQL. Do not edit `.mcp.json`
  to hide that error.
- Do not run `/eval-loop` until `_eval/GOLD.csv` has at least 20
  labelled rows (`in_class` or `out_class`).

## Session execution

- Issue independent tool calls in one turn. Wait only on true data
  dependence.
- Retry a failed call only when it is a flake. Cap retries at two. Do
  not retry a red test or a type error.
- Search first. Read only the span you need. Do not dump whole files.
- Background a full test suite, a long compile, or a sidecar restore.
  Use `scripts/worktree_agent.sh` for an isolated parallel task.
- Do not add a DAG scheduler, a knowledge graph, a message queue, or
  extra machines from a skill. Full text:
  `.claude/prompt-snippets/session-execution.md`.

# Coding Standards

- Write clean, readable, and maintainable code
- Follow language-specific conventions and idioms
- Use meaningful variable and function names
- Keep functions small and focused on a single responsibility
- Add comments only where the logic isn't self-evident
- Follow established patterns
- Never use ssh directly to connect; let the user handle this
- Never git push automatically by yourself
